# Fragment: the hatch's kernel only, layered over common.config and
# diskless.config, in that order (see default.nix).
#
# common.config gives every role no IP stack and no network device, so that a
# guest cannot reach the network is a property of its kernel. The hatch is the
# one exception, and the only one: it is the fleet's way out, fetching what
# consumers name — their registries, their key brokers — and it holds no
# applicant data and no seal key. Every other role keeps the property, and its
# measurement says so.
#
# What it gets is the least that carries TCP and UDP over one virtio NIC:
# IPv4, the virtio-net driver, and the kernel's own DHCP client, which the
# measured command line starts with `ip=dhcp` before PID 1 runs — so nothing in
# userspace configures the network, and the address is the host's DHCP answer.
# The resolver is the image's own /etc/resolv.conf, not the answer's.
#
# defconfig turns much more on beneath INET, and common.config's `INET is not
# set` was what kept it off. Turning INET back on would bring it back, so what
# it would bring is turned off here by name: no IPv6, no packet filter or
# tunnel, no multicast or policy routing, no IPsec, no other device driver.
CONFIG_INET=y
CONFIG_NETDEVICES=y
CONFIG_NET_CORE=y
CONFIG_VIRTIO_NET=y
CONFIG_IP_PNP=y
CONFIG_IP_PNP_DHCP=y
# CONFIG_IP_PNP_BOOTP is not set
# CONFIG_IP_PNP_RARP is not set

# CONFIG_IPV6 is not set
# CONFIG_NETFILTER is not set
# CONFIG_IP_MULTICAST is not set
# CONFIG_IP_ADVANCED_ROUTER is not set
# CONFIG_NET_IPIP is not set
# CONFIG_NET_IPGRE_DEMUX is not set
# CONFIG_NET_IPVTI is not set
# CONFIG_NET_FOU is not set
# CONFIG_INET_AH is not set
# CONFIG_INET_ESP is not set
# CONFIG_INET_IPCOMP is not set
# CONFIG_INET_DIAG is not set
# CONFIG_XFRM_USER is not set
# CONFIG_NET_KEY is not set
# CONFIG_SYN_COOKIES is not set
# CONFIG_NET_SCHED is not set
# CONFIG_NET_CLS_ACT is not set
# CONFIG_BRIDGE is not set
# CONFIG_VLAN_8021Q is not set
# CONFIG_NETLABEL is not set
# CONFIG_DNS_RESOLVER is not set

# Of the network devices, virtio-net alone.
# CONFIG_ETHERNET is not set
# CONFIG_WLAN is not set
# CONFIG_PPP is not set
# CONFIG_SLIP is not set
# CONFIG_TUN is not set
# CONFIG_MACVLAN is not set
# CONFIG_VXLAN is not set
# CONFIG_NETCONSOLE is not set
# CONFIG_NET_FC is not set
# CONFIG_PHYLIB is not set
# CONFIG_MDIO_DEVICE is not set
